---
title: Review
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: Spaced retrieval practice over every exit criterion on the site, scheduled at expanding intervals so that each question comes back just as it is about to slip.
permalink: /review/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<div class="review-page" data-review-page>
  <h1>Review</h1>

  <p class="review-lead">
    Every written article ends with <a href="/topics/">exit criteria</a>: tasks you attempt cold, with worked
    answers. This page schedules those {{ reviewItems | length }} tasks so each one returns shortly before you would
    have forgotten it, drawn from across the curriculum rather than one article at a time.
  </p>

  <div class="review-stats" data-review-stats hidden>
    <div class="review-stat"><span class="review-stat-value" data-review-due>0</span><span class="review-stat-label">due now</span></div>
    <div class="review-stat"><span class="review-stat-value" data-review-learning>0</span><span class="review-stat-label">in progress</span></div>
    <div class="review-stat"><span class="review-stat-value" data-review-known>0</span><span class="review-stat-label">on long intervals</span></div>
    <div class="review-stat"><span class="review-stat-value" data-review-pool>0</span><span class="review-stat-label">in scope</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="review-loading" data-review-loading>Loading the deck…</p>

  <div class="review-message" data-review-empty hidden></div>

  <section class="review-session" data-review-session aria-live="polite" hidden>
    <p class="review-last" data-review-next aria-live="polite"></p>

    <div class="review-card">
      <p class="review-card-meta">
        <span data-review-position></span>
        <span class="review-card-source">
          <a href="/topics/" data-review-source-link></a><span data-review-lesson></span>
        </span>
      </p>

      <div class="review-task" data-review-task></div>

      <div class="review-actions" data-review-reveal-row>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-review-reveal>Show answer</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-review-skip>Skip</button>
        <span class="review-hint">Write your attempt down first.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="review-answer" data-review-answer hidden></div>

      <div class="review-grade" data-review-grade hidden>
        <p class="review-grade-prompt">How did the attempt go?</p>
        <div class="review-grade-buttons">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-grade="missed">Missed it</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-grade="hard">Got there, slowly</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-grade="got">Got it</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="review-message" data-review-done hidden></div>

  <details class="review-settings" data-review-settings hidden>
    <summary>Deck settings</summary>

    <fieldset class="review-scope">
      <legend>Draw questions from</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="review-scope" value="plan" data-review-scope> Articles I have ticked off in the <a href="/plan/">learning plan</a></label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="review-scope" value="all" data-review-scope> Every written article</label>
    </fieldset>

    <p class="review-reset-row">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-review-reset>Reset all review history</button>
    </p>
  </details>

  <section class="review-how">
    <h2>How the scheduling works</h2>

    <p>
      An item you get right moves to a longer interval; an item you miss goes back to the start. The intervals
      expand — one day, three, a week, sixteen days, five weeks, three months — because a retrieval that is
      slightly difficult does more than an easy one, and an item recalled without effort has been asked too soon.
    </p>

    <p>
      The queue is shuffled and avoids putting two questions from the same article next to each other where it can.
      Blocked practice, where you work everything on one topic together, produces better performance during the
      session and worse retention afterwards. Interleaving feels worse and is worth it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Grading yourself honestly is the part that decides whether any of this works. <em>Got there, slowly</em> exists
      so that the choice is not only between a clean success and a failure; use it whenever you needed a run-up,
      and the item will come back at the same interval rather than a longer one.
    </p>

    <p class="review-privacy">
      Review history lives in this browser and nowhere else. It is not sent anywhere, and it will not follow you
      to another device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <noscript>
    <p class="review-message">
      Review scheduling needs JavaScript. Without it, the exit criteria are still on the articles themselves —
      start from the <a href="/topics/">topics page</a>.
    </p>
  </noscript>
</div>
